From cce923569426d68ae4708834d45027eca9e79586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alhuda Khan <alhuda@research.digiscrypt.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:12:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tar: avoid signed left shift in base-256 getOctal()

In base-256 mode, getOctal() shifts the signed int8_t leading byte left
by 1 bit (`first <<= 1`) to discard the high flag bit before arithmetic
right-shifting (`first >>= 1`) to sign-extend the 7-bit payload. When bit 6
is set (negative base-256 values), shifting a negative signed value left
triggers undefined behavior under C99/C11 (-fsanitize=undefined).

Cast `first` to `(uint8_t)` before the left shift (`first = (uint8_t)first << 1;`)
while keeping `first` as `int8_t` so the subsequent `first >>= 1` sign-extension
remains unchanged.

Thanks!

Signed-off-by: Alhuda Khan <alhuda@research.digiscrypt.com>
Signed-off-by: Denys Vlasenko <vda.linux@googlemail.com>
---
 archival/libarchive/get_header_tar.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/archival/libarchive/get_header_tar.c b/archival/libarchive/get_header_tar.c
index 56ae8f2..4257ae3 100644
--- a/archival/libarchive/get_header_tar.c
+++ b/archival/libarchive/get_header_tar.c
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ static unsigned long long getOctal(char *str, int len)
 		 * NB: tarballs with NEGATIVE unix times encoded that way were seen!
 		 */
 		/* Sign-extend 7bit 'first' to 64bit 'v' (that is, using 6th bit as sign): */
-		first <<= 1;
+		first = (uint8_t)first << 1; /* placate UBSan (it doesn't like signed left shift here) */
 		first >>= 1; /* now 7th bit = 6th bit */
 		v = first;   /* sign-extend 8 bits to 64 */
 		while (--len != 0)
-- 
2.53.0

